WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.290
A doctor prescribes an antibiotic
that used to clear up an

2
00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:04.970
infection easily.

3
00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.690
Now, years later, it barely
touches the same kind of bacteria.

4
00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:13.530
Nobody in a laboratory changed
those bacteria on purpose.

5
00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.390
So what did change them?

6
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.990
In this mission, you'll see
where variation comes from,

7
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.190
including brand-new variation
caused by mutations.

8
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:26.230
You'll find out which individuals
are most likely to survive,

9
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.370
reproduce and pass on their alleles.

10
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.710
And you'll see how,
over many generations,

11
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.390
a whole population can change.

12
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.970
Your mission: explain how
bacteria become resistant to

13
00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:39.460
antibiotics.
